## =============================================================================
## te_platform/db/alembic.ini.template — Alembic's configuration file
## =============================================================================
## GUIDE STEP   5.3
## PURPOSE      Alembic (the migration tool) reads a file named alembic.ini to
##              find its scripts folder and logging settings. This template
##              becomes te_platform/db/alembic.ini.
## USED BY      the `alembic` command, run by the one-shot `migrate` service in
##              Compose (`alembic -c te_platform/db/alembic.ini upgrade head`).
## DEPENDS ON   migrations/env.py (which supplies the database URL and tables).
## WHY          The database URL is deliberately NOT written here: env.py reads
##              it from Settings.migration_database_url (an environment
##              variable / Docker secret), so no password is ever committed.
## ACTIVATE     Copy this template to te_platform/db/alembic.ini and uncomment
##              it. Do NOT run `alembic init`: the standard files it would
##              create are already shipped (migrations/README.md). Commands
##              then use `alembic -c te_platform/db/alembic.ini ...`.
## =============================================================================

