##
## Guide 5.3
## [ ] 1. An [alembic] section with three keys: script_location, the
##        migrations folder next to the ini file,
##          | script_location = %(here)s/migrations
##        file_template, so new migration files start with the date (an ini
##        file needs %% for a literal %), and prepend_sys_path = .
## [ ] 2. No sqlalchemy.url line: env.py supplies the URL (header WHY).
## [ ] 3. The logging sections: [loggers] with keys root,sqlalchemy,alembic;
##        [handlers] console; [formatters] generic; then [logger_root]
##        (WARNING, console handler), [logger_sqlalchemy] (WARNING,
##        qualname sqlalchemy.engine), [logger_alembic] (INFO),
##        [handler_console] (StreamHandler on sys.stderr) and
##        [formatter_generic].
## [ ] 4. A [post_write_hooks] section: after writing a new migration,
##        Alembic runs ruff on it (`check --fix`, then `format`), so a
##        generated file passes the CI lint job. `exec` runs the `ruff` of
##        the environment that runs alembic (`uv run` puts .venv/bin first).
##          | hooks = ruff_fix, ruff_format
##          | ruff_fix.type = exec
## [ ] 5. Check, with migrations/env.py active (migrations/README.md):
##          | uv run alembic -c te_platform/db/alembic.ini upgrade head
##        then `downgrade -1` and `upgrade head` again (guide 5.3).
##
## Stuck, or want to compare? The SOLUTION below is the complete reference
## code. Uncomment it only if you decide to use it as it is.

